# Confidential investor material. Still ignored with the repository private:
# these are large binaries the site never serves, and the numbers inside them
# reach the dashboard as extracted data in dashboard-data.json, not as files.
*.docx
*.xlsx
*.pdf

# Local-only holding area for content pulled off the site temporarily.
.content-archive/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE FIVE DATA FILES ARE IGNORED AGAIN, AND THIS TIME NOTHING RESTS ON IT.
#
# dashboard-data.json, crm-data.json, operator-data.json, tasks-data.json and
# competitor-data.json hold real deal names, sponsor names, investor firms,
# conversation notes, and an internal read on named rival firms.
# They were briefly committed, which forced this repository private and left a
# standing hazard: make it public again without purging history and every one
# of those names is published.
#
# That hazard is gone rather than managed. The live copies now live in Vercel
# storage — the document index in Blob, the records in Redis — put there by
# tools/publish.py. The copies here are working files and seeds, and git does
# not carry them. THE REPOSITORY CAN BE PUBLIC AGAIN and holds only code.
#
# What has NOT changed: the deployed dashboard, /api/documents and
# /api/records all still answer anyone with the URL. Moving the data out of
# git changed where it lives and who can lose it, not who can read it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
dashboard-data.json
dashboard-data.*.json
deals-data.json
deals-data.*.json
crm-data.json
crm-data.*.json
operator-data.json
operator-data.*.json
tasks-data.json
tasks-data.*.json
competitor-data.json
competitor-data.*.json

# Forwarded-email intake staging for the investor CRM. Local working area,
# not records — the records it produces land in crm-data.json.
crm-inbox/

# Node dependencies for the /api/agent function.
node_modules/

# The local path to the OneDrive folder the dashboard mirrors. Machine-specific
# — it names one person's home directory, so the script reads it and git does
# not carry it.
tools/snapshot-source.txt

# Local Claude Code settings and dev-server config. Machine-specific.
.claude/

# Credentials for the serverless functions. These live in the Vercel project's
# environment variables and must never be in a file here — this repository is
# public again. BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN and KV_REST_API_TOKEN can each rewrite
# what the whole team reads; DASHBOARD_WRITE_KEY is the lock in front of them.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
